{
  "comment": "The license texts the app bundle carries (THIRD_PARTY.md). tools/bundle-licenses.py copies them at build time from where the build fetched them into Minato.app/Licenses/<component>/, with Licenses/licenses.json as the index; tools/license-check.py checks a built bundle against THIRD_PARTY.md. 'sections': when the app embeds a section of THIRD_PARTY.md: always, with this framework in the bundle's Frameworks/, or never. 'rows': the first cells of THIRD_PARTY.md's table rows the component covers. 'texts': <root>:<path>; roots: sources = build/sources, moltenvk = build/moltenvk, angle = ANGLE's checkout in build/angle/angle at the pins of third_party/sources.json (tools/build-angle.sh --fetch), repo = the repository, ndk = the NDK (ANDROID_NDK, as tools/build-bionic.sh). A text may take only some lines ('lines': [first, last]). 'none': why nothing of the component is in the binary. ART and its libraries are 'always' since ADR-0033 d2 puts ART's APEXes into every build; their build tools stay 'never'. So are the framework's sources and the graphics sources since ADR-0039 c4 puts framework.jar, framework-res, platform.xml, libandroid_runtime.so and hwui's libraries into every build; the framework's build tools stay 'never'. A project without a license text of its own at the tag takes the repository's Apache-2.0 text. A path with a slash is a file in the bundle: test 2's APKs go into a benchmark build together (tools/embed-benchmark.sh), so their section's rule names one of them.",
  "sections": {
    "Guest libc": "always",
    "Graphics: ANGLE": "libGLESv2.framework",
    "Graphics: MoltenVK": "MoltenVK.framework",
    "Parity benchmark": "MinatoBench.framework",
    "ART and its libraries": "always",
    "Build tools for ART": "never",
    "Build tools for the framework": "never",
    "Framework sources": "always",
    "Graphics sources": "always",
    "Guest fonts": "always",
    "Test 2 with Godot": "MinatoGodot.framework",
    "Test 2's APKs": "Benchmark/godot-bench-vulkan.apk",
    "Build tools for the formats": "never",
    "References without adopted code": "never"
  },
